WEBVTT

00:00:07.452 --> 00:00:11.673
A trip to Bavaria.

00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:16.154
Going abroad.

00:00:16.214 --> 00:00:22.986
Pete, Josephine is talking to you.

00:00:23.046 --> 00:00:25.066
Our daughter, remember?

00:00:25.126 --> 00:00:27.847
Yes dear, no sugar, thank you.

00:00:27.907 --> 00:00:28.947
What?

00:00:29.007 --> 00:00:32.584
She's trying to tell you something.

00:00:32.644 --> 00:00:34.330
What's the point?

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.101
My name is Heidi.

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:37.761
She lives near Munich.

00:00:37.821 --> 00:00:39.351
Oh, that's nice.

00:00:39.411 --> 00:00:42.852
That's where the doctor Burfest takes place.

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:45.493
Don't you mean the Oktoberfest?

00:00:45.553 --> 00:00:47.463
That's worth her said Nancy.

00:00:47.523 --> 00:00:51.534
Lots of lovely strong German men drinking beer.

00:00:51.594 --> 00:00:55.605
I don't see what that's got to do with Josie's trip to Germany.

00:00:55.665 --> 00:01:00.596
Anyway, Josie, try making contact with your father again, please.

00:01:00.656 --> 00:01:03.478
Put Heidi's photo in front of his nose.

00:01:03.498 --> 00:01:04.649
Dad.

00:01:04.709 --> 00:01:06.780
No more toast, thank you.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.382
Look at this.

00:01:08.441 --> 00:01:10.493
She's nice, isn't she?

00:01:10.553 --> 00:01:12.154
Very nice.

00:01:12.214 --> 00:01:13.585
And of yours.

00:01:13.645 --> 00:01:16.217
Her name's Heidi, she's German.

00:01:16.277 --> 00:01:18.438
I'm going to visit her in Germany.

00:01:18.498 --> 00:01:19.330
Nice.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:21.851
Did you hear what Josie said?

00:01:21.911 --> 00:01:25.870
And to put that newspaper down.

00:01:25.929 --> 00:01:29.027
You want to have a real conversation with you.

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:40.235
Oh, there's more life in a plastic bag, but Josie is going to stay with her German exchange partner near Munich for two months in the summer holidays.

00:01:40.295 --> 00:01:41.687
Well, that's nice.

00:01:41.746 --> 00:01:43.688
Wait a minute.

00:01:43.748 --> 00:01:45.298
Munich?

00:01:45.358 --> 00:01:47.010
That's in Germany.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.221
At last, welcome back to our planet.

00:01:50.261 --> 00:01:51.812
Leave me up, Scotty.

00:01:51.872 --> 00:01:54.013
Oh, who is Scotty?

00:01:54.073 --> 00:01:56.935
I once had a budgie called Scotty.

00:01:56.995 --> 00:01:58.716
He was very clever.

00:01:58.776 --> 00:02:00.226
He could speak.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:03.628
I taught him to say, close the window.

00:02:03.688 --> 00:02:05.139
Close the window.

00:02:05.199 --> 00:02:08.751
One day I forgot and he flew out the window.

00:02:08.771 --> 00:02:11.192
Be quiet please mum.

00:02:11.252 --> 00:02:12.483
Germany.

00:02:12.543 --> 00:02:14.604
Yes, Germany.

00:02:14.664 --> 00:02:16.616
Munich is in Germany.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.178
But...

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.389
There are Germans in Germany.

00:02:20.449 --> 00:02:24.302
Your knowledge of European geography is very impressive.

00:02:24.362 --> 00:02:26.374
You should be on Mastermind.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:27.475
Yes, Dad.

00:02:27.535 --> 00:02:30.548
There are lots of Germans in Germany.

00:02:30.608 --> 00:02:33.980
I'm going to stay with a German family for two months.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:34.470
But...

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:35.251
But...

00:02:35.311 --> 00:02:37.582
They speak German.

00:02:37.642 --> 00:02:41.985
Gosh, is there no limit to my husband's intelligence?

00:02:42.045 --> 00:02:46.367
Why don't you go to a nice country, a sensible country?

00:02:46.427 --> 00:02:48.377
What do you suggest, dearest?

00:02:48.437 --> 00:02:55.140
Well, America or Canada or even Gibraltar?

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.262
I want to improve my German dad.

00:02:58.322 --> 00:03:00.573
All those countries speak English.

00:03:00.633 --> 00:03:04.494
Yes, but why do you want to learn another language?

00:03:04.554 --> 00:03:06.305
Everyone speaks English.

00:03:06.365 --> 00:03:09.466
I'm learning German at school, remember?

00:03:09.526 --> 00:03:11.758
I went to Germany once.

00:03:11.818 --> 00:03:13.538
I didn't know that.

00:03:13.598 --> 00:03:14.389
When?

00:03:14.449 --> 00:03:16.430
When the Kaiser was still alive?

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:19.591
I'm not sure when it was a long time ago.

00:03:19.611 --> 00:03:22.362
I think it was Germany.

00:03:22.422 --> 00:03:25.294
Or maybe it was the Isle of Wight.

00:03:25.354 --> 00:03:33.568
It looked very foreign, lots of bicycles and hills, and people with sunglasses and red faces.

00:03:33.628 --> 00:03:36.711
Anyway, Mom says I can go to Germany.

00:03:36.771 --> 00:03:38.293
It's with the school.

00:03:38.353 --> 00:03:39.464
Nothing can happen.

00:03:39.484 --> 00:03:40.705
I know.

00:03:40.725 --> 00:03:43.188
We can come and visit you.

00:03:43.248 --> 00:03:46.371
We can have a holiday in Germany too.

00:03:46.431 --> 00:03:48.554
Not so fast, Mom.

00:03:48.614 --> 00:03:50.736
I don't think Josie was.

00:03:50.756 --> 00:03:52.108
That's awesome.

00:03:52.168 --> 00:03:54.570
Yes, that's a great idea.

00:03:54.629 --> 00:03:58.946
Why not come near the end and then we can visit some places together?

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.607
What a good idea!

00:04:00.627 --> 00:04:02.760
Don't you think so, Pete?

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:05.696
You can meet Heidi and her father.

00:04:05.756 --> 00:04:07.358
That's settled then.

00:04:07.418 --> 00:04:08.659
We're coming.

00:04:08.719 --> 00:04:12.970
Perhaps Heidi's father can find us a cheap hotel for a few days.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.091
Cool.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.321
I can get Heidi to ask her father.

00:04:16.381 --> 00:04:18.152
I'm sure he knows some places.

00:04:18.212 --> 00:04:20.402
A trip to Germany.

00:04:20.462 --> 00:04:21.963
How exciting.

00:04:22.023 --> 00:04:26.014
It's our first trip abroad for over 15 years.

00:04:26.074 --> 00:04:27.474
No, it's not.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:29.675
We went to Calais two years ago.

00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:31.856
That's not exactly true.

00:04:31.916 --> 00:04:35.520
You forgot your passport and we couldn't enter France.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:39.613
All we saw was the port from the ferry and then we came back again.

00:04:39.673 --> 00:04:41.054
Yes, I forgot.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:43.456
Why did you marry him, Nancy?

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:45.178
I liked Andrew.

00:04:45.238 --> 00:04:47.380
He sells vacuum clean.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.841
I met his wife.

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:50.752
She left him in January.

00:04:50.812 --> 00:04:53.615
Now she lives with the ice cream man.

00:04:53.675 --> 00:04:56.257
Andrew's alone at home with his hovers.

00:04:56.317 --> 00:04:57.792
You too.

00:04:57.852 --> 00:05:01.201
Josie, what present are you taking?

00:05:01.261 --> 00:05:03.134
What about a book of jokes?

00:05:03.194 --> 00:05:05.391
You know Germans have no sense of humour.

00:05:05.451 --> 00:05:07.586
Don't be stupid, Dad.

00:05:07.646 --> 00:05:08.957
Maybe a towel?

00:05:09.017 --> 00:05:09.808
Sorry.

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:16.612
It's a fact that on holidays, Germans always get up early in the morning to put their towels on the sunbeds next to the pool.

00:05:16.672 --> 00:05:18.403
Don't listen to your father.

00:05:18.463 --> 00:05:21.796
He lives in his own fantasy world of stereotypes.

00:05:21.856 --> 00:05:24.888
Perhaps some typical English food.

00:05:24.948 --> 00:05:29.410
You know things like tea and marmite food.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:31.737
That's a great idea, Grand.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:35.323
Josie, make sure you don't mention the war.

00:05:35.343 --> 00:05:36.413
Stop it.

00:05:36.473 --> 00:05:39.154
We're in the European Union now.

00:05:39.214 --> 00:05:40.224
I'm not.

00:05:40.284 --> 00:05:42.475
I never wanted to join.

00:05:42.535 --> 00:05:43.916
Come on Boris.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.026
Walkies.

00:05:45.086 --> 00:05:49.348
Let's go and breathe some good English air together.

00:05:49.408 --> 00:05:51.370
Oh, dear.

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:55.452
I'm not so sure it's a good idea to take Dad to Germany, Mum.

00:05:55.512 --> 00:05:56.572
Yes, I know.

00:05:56.592 --> 00:05:59.413
But he doesn't really mean what he says.

00:05:59.473 --> 00:06:01.404
He's just trying to be funny.

00:06:01.464 --> 00:06:03.835
But he never says anything that is funny.

00:06:03.895 --> 00:06:04.775
No.

00:06:04.835 --> 00:06:06.156
I know.

00:06:06.216 --> 00:06:12.158
Sad, really, isn't it?

00:06:12.218 --> 00:06:19.082
Bavaria, here we come.

00:06:19.142 --> 00:06:22.385
Why didn't we fly?

00:06:22.445 --> 00:06:28.307
This ferry journey is so boring, and Port Boris is locked in the car.

00:06:28.367 --> 00:06:29.877
I hope he's all right.

00:06:29.937 --> 00:06:31.667
Of course he is.

00:06:31.727 --> 00:06:33.788
It's nice to go by ferry.

00:06:33.848 --> 00:06:36.388
A real sense of adventure.

00:06:36.448 --> 00:06:39.749
We English are famous for RC captains.

00:06:39.809 --> 00:06:42.410
So Walter Raleigh.

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:45.834
Captain Cook.

00:06:45.894 --> 00:06:48.670
Christopher Columbus.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:51.493
Christopher Columbus was Italian.

00:06:51.553 --> 00:06:54.576
Don't be ridiculous, Italian.

00:06:54.636 --> 00:06:56.759
He can't be Italian.

00:06:56.819 --> 00:07:01.225
What are the Italians given the world besides pizza and ice cream?

00:07:01.284 --> 00:07:03.646
I think mum's right, Pete.

00:07:03.706 --> 00:07:06.486
No, anyway.

00:07:06.546 --> 00:07:11.469
Sir Francis Chichester, the first man to sail around the world alone.

00:07:11.529 --> 00:07:12.440
All right.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:15.212
All right, you made your point.

00:07:15.272 --> 00:07:20.235
Anyway, not long now, I hope.

00:07:20.295 --> 00:07:26.449
And please, Josie is having such a nice time with the family.

00:07:26.509 --> 00:07:30.872
I'm really looking forward to seeing her again and meeting the family, aren't you?

00:07:30.932 --> 00:07:33.636
Yes, but...

00:07:33.696 --> 00:07:37.370
Oh, it's so exciting.

00:07:37.429 --> 00:07:39.511
It makes me feel tipsy.

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:43.023
Everything is going from side to side.

00:07:43.083 --> 00:07:45.214
To see is very rough.

00:07:45.273 --> 00:07:47.565
I don't like it too much.

00:07:47.625 --> 00:07:49.296
Oh, my stomach.

00:07:49.356 --> 00:07:54.049
It's very nice of Heidi's father to say we can stay in his house.

00:07:54.109 --> 00:07:55.840
Yes, it is.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:59.912
The Germans are such nice people, don't you agree, Pete?

00:07:59.972 --> 00:08:04.465
What's the name of Joseph's German family?

00:08:04.524 --> 00:08:06.886
What's his first name?

00:08:06.946 --> 00:08:08.907
And where is Mrs. Fokker?

00:08:08.967 --> 00:08:10.988
I don't know his Christian name.

00:08:11.048 --> 00:08:13.409
Germans are much more formal, Pete.

00:08:13.469 --> 00:08:15.380
I read it in the guidebook.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:17.962
I don't know where Heidi's mother is.

00:08:18.022 --> 00:08:19.873
Maybe they're divorced.

00:08:19.933 --> 00:08:23.295
I wouldn't be surprised with a name like that.

00:08:23.355 --> 00:08:25.756
I wonder if he fought in the war.

00:08:25.816 --> 00:08:27.186
I must ask him.

00:08:27.246 --> 00:08:28.707
Please don't.

00:08:28.767 --> 00:08:31.028
Anyway, he isn't old enough.

00:08:31.088 --> 00:08:34.709
Don't forget that the war finished over 60 years ago.

00:08:34.729 --> 00:08:39.111
I don't feel too well.

00:08:39.171 --> 00:08:41.442
My stomach doesn't like it.

00:08:41.502 --> 00:08:43.533
Oh, my stomach.

00:08:43.593 --> 00:08:44.384
Don't worry.

00:08:44.444 --> 00:08:45.414
It's OK.

00:08:45.474 --> 00:08:46.154
Here.

00:08:46.214 --> 00:08:48.425
Have a peanut butter sandwich.

00:08:48.485 --> 00:08:50.436
They taste great.

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:54.476
Here are some chocolate biscuits too.

00:08:54.536 --> 00:09:00.227
No, I can't eat anything.

00:09:00.287 --> 00:09:03.549
Soon be there, don't worry.

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:05.029
Do you want some coke?

00:09:05.089 --> 00:09:06.440
No, thank you.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.461
I just want to sit quietly.

00:09:08.521 --> 00:09:10.712
Shall I get you an ice cream?

00:09:10.772 --> 00:09:13.354
I want to go up on deck.

00:09:13.414 --> 00:09:15.325
Smell the sea air.

00:09:15.385 --> 00:09:16.865
Don't fall overboard.

00:09:16.885 --> 00:09:18.936
See you later.

00:09:18.997 --> 00:09:22.248
Why didn't we fly, Pete?

00:09:22.308 --> 00:09:23.939
I feel awful.

00:09:23.999 --> 00:09:26.134
Another sandwich, dear.

00:09:26.194 --> 00:09:28.160
Enjoying the exhibit.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.822
Can it isn't Stulham?

00:09:29.882 --> 00:09:30.713
What?

00:09:30.773 --> 00:09:32.606
Are you all right?

00:09:32.666 --> 00:09:34.698
Do you have a speech problem?

00:09:34.758 --> 00:09:36.440
Enjoying the exhibit.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.411
Can it isn't Stulham?

00:09:38.472 --> 00:09:41.024
Lovely day, yes.

00:09:41.084 --> 00:09:43.557
Can't you speak a proper language?

00:09:43.577 --> 00:09:45.478
It's yours.

00:09:45.538 --> 00:09:47.888
What did he want?

00:09:47.948 --> 00:09:49.830
I have no idea.

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:51.960
He was speaking in a funny language.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:53.501
French, I think.

00:09:53.561 --> 00:09:55.362
It wasn't French.

00:09:55.422 --> 00:09:56.933
He spoke German.

00:09:56.993 --> 00:09:58.084
He's German.

00:09:58.124 --> 00:09:59.144
French, German.

00:09:59.204 --> 00:10:01.636
It's all the same.

00:10:01.696 --> 00:10:07.338
Pete, do you think it a good idea to come by car?

00:10:07.398 --> 00:10:09.409
You know the problems we have with it.

00:10:09.469 --> 00:10:13.091
It's so old and it's not very reliable.

00:10:13.151 --> 00:10:16.568
I checked everything very carefully.

00:10:16.627 --> 00:10:19.813
I'm sure nothing can go wrong.

00:10:19.873 --> 00:10:22.224
Sorry.

00:10:22.284 --> 00:10:25.745
How long is the journey to Bavaria?

00:10:25.805 --> 00:10:27.376
Only a few hours.

00:10:27.436 --> 00:10:28.666
It's all motorway.

00:10:28.726 --> 00:10:32.117
You know they drive on the other side of the road.

00:10:32.177 --> 00:10:33.788
Are you all right?

00:10:33.848 --> 00:10:35.168
You don't look well.

00:10:35.228 --> 00:10:37.348
Of course I'm all right.

00:10:37.408 --> 00:10:40.237
Yes, I know they drive on the left.

00:10:40.297 --> 00:10:41.888
I'm not totally stupid.

00:10:41.948 --> 00:10:44.279
Oh dear, of course you're not.

00:10:44.339 --> 00:10:46.890
It can't be difficult.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.642
Trust me.

00:10:49.702 --> 00:10:51.842
You look a bit green.

00:10:51.902 --> 00:10:54.613
Are you sure you're okay?

00:10:54.673 --> 00:10:57.404
Just a bit of indigestion.

00:10:57.464 --> 00:10:59.385
Oh, I think.

00:10:59.445 --> 00:11:00.576
Oh dear.

00:11:00.636 --> 00:11:04.668
I think I ate too many peanut butter sandwiches.

00:11:04.728 --> 00:11:09.460
I think I need to go to the toilet.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:13.130
I don't feel too well.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:14.821
Do you need some help?

00:11:14.881 --> 00:11:16.142
No, no dear.

00:11:16.202 --> 00:11:17.822
It's just a bit of in...

00:11:17.882 --> 00:11:19.883
Did just...

00:11:19.943 --> 00:11:21.943
Oh, careful dear.

00:11:22.003 --> 00:11:24.194
The boat is swaying a lot.

00:11:24.254 --> 00:11:26.074
Sorry, madam.

00:11:26.134 --> 00:11:27.345
Sorry.

00:11:27.385 --> 00:11:27.925
Hello, Pete.

00:11:27.985 --> 00:11:28.945
Isn't it fun?

00:11:29.005 --> 00:11:32.560
Are you all right?

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:36.375
Hello, Nancy.

00:11:36.435 --> 00:11:38.868
Pete looks as white as a sheet.

00:11:38.928 --> 00:11:42.871
Poor Lord Nelson is not feeling too well.

00:11:42.931 --> 00:11:44.852
Ah, he's got noise.

00:11:44.912 --> 00:11:46.894
Look, it's Pete.

00:11:46.954 --> 00:11:49.586
He fell over the table and...

00:11:49.647 --> 00:11:52.089
Oh, where is he?

00:11:52.149 --> 00:11:53.380
Look, Mum.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:54.561
The coast.

00:11:54.621 --> 00:11:56.072
I can see the coast.

00:11:56.132 --> 00:11:57.674
We're almost there.

00:11:57.734 --> 00:11:58.985
Where's Pete?

00:11:59.045 --> 00:12:02.008
We have to go downstairs to the car.

00:12:02.068 --> 00:12:05.369
I think that's him in the corner over there.

00:12:05.429 --> 00:12:07.610
Leave him for a few minutes.

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.650
I think he's fallen asleep.

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:12.712
It's nice to have a bit of peace and quiet.

00:12:12.772 --> 00:12:15.012
We could leave him there, Nancy.

00:12:15.072 --> 00:12:17.493
What a terrible thought, Marley.

00:12:17.553 --> 00:12:19.444
We can't do that.

00:12:19.504 --> 00:12:21.054
Can we?

00:12:21.114 --> 00:12:22.865
I suppose not.

00:12:22.925 --> 00:12:28.257
But it's a nice idea.

00:12:28.317 --> 00:12:34.906
On the road.

00:12:34.966 --> 00:12:40.549
What's the matter with these bloody Germans?

00:12:40.609 --> 00:12:44.484
They are crazy as the end of the world comes.

00:12:44.544 --> 00:12:46.316
Look out!

00:12:46.376 --> 00:12:50.002
Here's another one coming at supersonic speed.

00:12:50.062 --> 00:12:53.900
Be careful!

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:59.328
Where the bloody hell did that one come from?

00:12:59.388 --> 00:13:01.900
Why do they drive so fast?

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.381
It's dangerous.

00:13:03.441 --> 00:13:09.714
And why is every bloody German got either a bloody Mercedes or a bleeding BMW?

00:13:09.774 --> 00:13:11.536
Who won the war anyway?

00:13:11.596 --> 00:13:13.296
It's exciting.

00:13:13.356 --> 00:13:15.458
They all look such fun.

00:13:15.518 --> 00:13:18.239
Why can't we go any faster?

00:13:18.299 --> 00:13:20.630
I'm doing 55.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:24.573
This car wasn't built for speed.

00:13:24.633 --> 00:13:28.506
It wasn't built for comfort either.

00:13:28.566 --> 00:13:29.698
All leg room.

00:13:29.758 --> 00:13:31.429
All relaxation.

00:13:31.489 --> 00:13:36.976
All right, all right, don't keep on.

00:13:37.036 --> 00:13:43.062
