I'm sorry about my husband.

00:26:34.873 --> 00:26:37.814
Oh, I rule German men like you.

00:26:37.874 --> 00:26:38.815
Mother!

00:26:38.875 --> 00:26:39.705
Come on.

00:26:39.765 --> 00:26:41.286
Come and sit in the garden.

00:26:41.346 --> 00:26:43.127
The weather is lovely today.

00:26:43.187 --> 00:26:44.448
How was the journey?

00:26:44.508 --> 00:26:46.539
Very, very long.

00:26:46.599 --> 00:26:48.480
But that's another story.

00:26:48.540 --> 00:26:50.691
You have a wonderful house.

00:26:50.751 --> 00:26:52.092
Thank you so much.

00:26:52.153 --> 00:26:53.204
Come on, ladies.

00:26:53.264 --> 00:26:54.175
Sit next to me.

00:26:54.195 --> 00:26:56.707
Come and see my bedroom first, Mum.

00:26:56.767 --> 00:26:57.418
Grand?

00:26:57.478 --> 00:26:58.739
It's awesome.

00:26:58.759 --> 00:27:00.211
I have my own bathroom.

00:27:00.271 --> 00:27:01.782
Alright, Josie.

00:27:01.842 --> 00:27:04.486
You stay here, Pete, and look after Boris.

00:27:04.546 --> 00:27:07.909
And make sure you behave.

00:27:07.929 --> 00:27:08.880
Yes, dear.

00:27:08.940 --> 00:27:10.602
Help yourself to a drink.

00:27:10.662 --> 00:27:11.780
Thank you.

00:27:11.840 --> 00:27:14.479
You are all welcome to stay in my house.

00:27:14.539 --> 00:27:19.240
That's very nice of you, Mr. Her.

00:27:19.300 --> 00:27:22.032
A deadlift.

00:27:22.092 --> 00:27:23.222
Oh, sorry.

00:27:23.282 --> 00:27:24.933
A deadlift.

00:27:24.993 --> 00:27:28.844
You can do day trips to lots of famous places from here.

00:27:28.904 --> 00:27:30.695
Is that your car in the drive?

00:27:30.755 --> 00:27:31.966
Ah, yes.

00:27:32.026 --> 00:27:34.026
And you drove all this way in that.

00:27:34.086 --> 00:27:37.238
Yes, it's a solid British car.

00:27:37.298 --> 00:27:39.278
They don't make them like that anymore.

00:27:39.338 --> 00:27:41.175
I'm pleased to hear that.

00:27:41.235 --> 00:27:43.094
I'm only joking.

00:27:43.154 --> 00:27:46.756
I know you English like a dry sense of humour.

00:27:46.816 --> 00:27:50.195
You can use my car while you are here.

00:27:50.255 --> 00:27:51.946
Take the BMW.

00:27:52.006 --> 00:27:54.108
It's in the garage most of the time.

00:27:54.168 --> 00:27:55.729
I like to go by bicycle.

00:27:55.789 --> 00:27:59.211
Much healthier and better for the environment, don't you agree?

00:27:59.271 --> 00:28:01.173
Yes, I suppose so.

00:28:01.233 --> 00:28:02.974
You have a BMW?

00:28:03.034 --> 00:28:05.175
Yes, a nice German car.

00:28:05.236 --> 00:28:06.666
Very reliable.

00:28:06.726 --> 00:28:09.238
It's too big for just Heidi and myself.

00:28:09.298 --> 00:28:10.799
You must try it.

00:28:10.860 --> 00:28:11.940
Thank you.

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:15.223
Anyway, I just want to finish my swimming for the day.

00:28:15.283 --> 00:28:16.854
Please join me.

00:28:16.914 --> 00:28:20.188
Looking at you, I think you need some exercise.

00:28:20.248 --> 00:28:23.210
You don't want a heart attack, do you?

00:28:23.270 --> 00:28:24.551
Sorry.

00:28:24.611 --> 00:28:26.373
German humour.

00:28:26.433 --> 00:28:27.534
No, thank you.

00:28:27.594 --> 00:28:28.594
Long journey.

00:28:28.654 --> 00:28:30.806
No swimming costume.

00:28:30.866 --> 00:28:32.538
Can't swim.

00:28:32.598 --> 00:28:34.400
Bad leg.

00:28:34.460 --> 00:28:35.621
Okay.

00:28:35.681 --> 00:28:43.088
Back soon.

00:28:43.148 --> 00:28:50.714
Here's my room.

00:28:50.774 --> 00:28:51.424
Come in.

00:28:51.444 --> 00:28:54.846
Oh, wonderful.

00:28:54.906 --> 00:28:56.968
Balcony as well.

00:28:57.028 --> 00:28:59.980
Let me look.

00:29:00.040 --> 00:29:04.403
Your father is very young.

00:29:04.463 --> 00:29:06.324
Fit, Heidi.

00:29:06.384 --> 00:29:07.805
He likes to keep fit.

00:29:07.865 --> 00:29:12.092
He always says to me, help somebody, help somebody.

00:29:12.152 --> 00:29:16.108
Is that what I think it is?

00:29:16.128 --> 00:29:19.552
I couldn't leave him at home myself.

00:29:19.612 --> 00:29:21.894
Oh, it's Robbie.

00:29:21.954 --> 00:29:23.826
Oh, he's so sweet.

00:29:23.886 --> 00:29:26.421
Come here, little thing.

00:29:26.481 --> 00:29:28.726
My father likes him too.

00:29:28.786 --> 00:29:30.757
He lets him run around the house.

00:29:30.817 --> 00:29:33.218
I hid him in my handbag on the journey.

00:29:33.278 --> 00:29:34.529
It wasn't easy.

00:29:34.589 --> 00:29:37.471
And at school, the teachers wondered what the squeaking was.

00:29:37.531 --> 00:29:39.542
I'm sure they did.

00:29:39.602 --> 00:29:41.984
Let's go downstairs.

00:29:42.044 --> 00:29:46.036
It's in polite to stay here.

00:29:46.096 --> 00:29:50.208
Who's this, Josie?

00:29:50.269 --> 00:29:53.160
What do you mean, a gran?

00:29:53.220 --> 00:29:56.154
In the photo by the side of your bed.

00:29:56.214 --> 00:30:00.296
Just a friend, not important.

00:30:00.356 --> 00:30:01.316
That's Mike.

00:30:01.376 --> 00:30:02.937
He'd up it, Heidi.

00:30:02.997 --> 00:30:05.798
Oh, I was young many years ago.

00:30:05.858 --> 00:30:08.319
It's nice to have a friend.

00:30:08.379 --> 00:30:09.829
Is he nice?

00:30:09.889 --> 00:30:11.210
Yes.

00:30:11.270 --> 00:30:13.360
He's really fit.

00:30:13.420 --> 00:30:14.561
Really cool.

00:30:14.621 --> 00:30:15.591
Awesome.

00:30:15.651 --> 00:30:17.151
Don't tell mum and dad.

00:30:17.171 --> 00:30:18.372
Do you know what they're like?

00:30:18.432 --> 00:30:20.792
Your secret is safe with me.

00:30:20.852 --> 00:30:22.243
Thanks, Gran.

00:30:22.303 --> 00:30:25.306
He's in the class I'm in at Heidi's school.

00:30:25.366 --> 00:30:27.888
I hope he can come and stay with us in England.

00:30:27.948 --> 00:30:29.530
How romantic!

00:30:29.590 --> 00:30:32.123
I wish something like that happened to me.

00:30:32.143 --> 00:30:36.448
Maybe it will one day, but don't say anything to Mom and Dad.

00:30:36.508 --> 00:30:38.069
Particularly Dad.

00:30:38.129 --> 00:30:43.975
He'll blow a few.

00:30:44.035 --> 00:30:50.572
What an awesome car!

00:30:50.632 --> 00:30:52.344
I feel like the Queen!

00:30:52.404 --> 00:30:54.176
I think I'll wave to people!

00:30:54.236 --> 00:30:55.728
Hello!

00:30:55.788 --> 00:30:57.288
Hello!

00:30:57.348 --> 00:31:01.474
It's nice if Detleft and Lendy's BMW to us.

00:31:01.534 --> 00:31:04.606
Why can't we have a car like this, dear?

00:31:04.666 --> 00:31:10.002
It's not real driving, it's too quiet and comfortable.

00:31:10.062 --> 00:31:12.847
This heaps better than our piece of scrap metal.

00:31:12.908 --> 00:31:15.874
If you don't want to drive it, then I can drive it.

00:31:15.934 --> 00:31:18.218
No, no, it's okay.

00:31:18.278 --> 00:31:21.893
I can drive you sit and watch the scenery.

00:31:21.953 --> 00:31:24.213
Nancy?

00:31:24.273 --> 00:31:26.194
Yes, ma'am, what is it?

00:31:26.254 --> 00:31:28.364
I think I have a problem.

00:31:28.424 --> 00:31:30.125
What sort of problem?

00:31:30.185 --> 00:31:31.235
Where?

00:31:31.295 --> 00:31:34.476
Downstairs, if you know what I mean.

00:31:34.536 --> 00:31:35.707
Oh, dear!

00:31:35.767 --> 00:31:38.518
My bottom feels very hot.

00:31:38.578 --> 00:31:40.658
I think I need to stop.

00:31:40.718 --> 00:31:41.860
I heard that.

00:31:41.920 --> 00:31:43.211
Don't worry, you'll live.

00:31:43.271 --> 00:31:44.832
It's not funny, Pete.

00:31:44.892 --> 00:31:45.854
Yes, it is.

00:31:45.914 --> 00:31:48.416
I forgot to switch off her seat warmer.

00:31:48.476 --> 00:31:49.798
Sorry.

00:31:49.858 --> 00:31:52.800
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

00:31:52.860 --> 00:31:53.381
Who?

00:31:53.441 --> 00:31:54.132
Me?

00:31:54.192 --> 00:31:55.153
No.

00:31:55.213 --> 00:31:56.895
Of course I did this.

00:31:56.955 --> 00:31:58.706
Where are we going today?

00:31:58.766 --> 00:32:00.819
Somewhere interesting, I hope.

00:32:00.879 --> 00:32:02.980
Not a boring museum.

00:32:03.040 --> 00:32:06.492
I hope there's a McDonald's nearby, I'm starving.

00:32:06.552 --> 00:32:08.062
Noi Shranstein.

00:32:08.123 --> 00:32:09.773
Is that a disease?

00:32:09.833 --> 00:32:12.244
Is it something to do with pigs?

00:32:12.304 --> 00:32:13.944
No mum, it's not.

00:32:14.004 --> 00:32:16.746
That left said we must go and visit it.

00:32:16.806 --> 00:32:17.996
But what is it?

00:32:18.056 --> 00:32:20.407
It sounds mega boring to me.

00:32:20.467 --> 00:32:23.298
If you look out of the window, you can see it.

00:32:23.358 --> 00:32:24.378
Where?

00:32:24.438 --> 00:32:27.039
All I can see is a supermarket.

00:32:27.099 --> 00:32:30.260
No mum, over there.

00:32:30.320 --> 00:32:34.502
I didn't know they had Aldi in Germany as well.

00:32:34.562 --> 00:32:37.083
I always go shopping in Aldi.

00:32:37.143 --> 00:32:38.164
It's cheap.

00:32:38.224 --> 00:32:41.065
I bought three pairs of knickers for 99p.

00:32:41.085 --> 00:32:44.046
They weren't very good though.

00:32:44.106 --> 00:32:46.587
I clean the windows with them now.

00:32:46.647 --> 00:32:48.668
Would you like a pair Nancy?

00:32:48.728 --> 00:32:50.529
No, thank you mum.

00:32:50.589 --> 00:32:52.750
Nancy isn't the size of an elephant.

00:32:52.810 --> 00:32:54.641
Be quiet Pete.

00:32:54.701 --> 00:32:56.972
Aldi is a German company.

00:32:57.032 --> 00:32:58.880
It's very famous here.

00:32:58.940 --> 00:33:00.576
It's German.

00:33:00.636 --> 00:33:02.167
I didn't know that.

00:33:02.227 --> 00:33:05.587
That's the last time we go shopping there in England.

00:33:05.647 --> 00:33:08.888
Next time we can go to the other cheap supermarket.

00:33:08.948 --> 00:33:10.028
What's it called?

00:33:10.088 --> 00:33:11.359
Do you mean little?

00:33:11.419 --> 00:33:12.689
Because that's awesome.

00:33:12.709 --> 00:33:15.430
Yes, that's the one.

00:33:15.490 --> 00:33:16.920
Yes.

00:33:16.980 --> 00:33:18.810
Alright dear.

00:33:18.870 --> 00:33:23.052
All I can see is a castle, a tall white building.

00:33:23.112 --> 00:33:25.492
It looks like the one in Disney World.

00:33:25.552 --> 00:33:26.333
Yes.

00:33:26.393 --> 00:33:27.483
That's it.

00:33:27.543 --> 00:33:29.244
We're going there.

00:33:29.304 --> 00:33:30.954
Is it an amusement park?

00:33:31.014 --> 00:33:31.794
Cool.

00:33:31.854 --> 00:33:34.295
We could go on the roller coaster.

00:33:34.355 --> 00:33:37.476
I hope they have one that does loop the loop.

00:33:37.536 --> 00:33:39.947
I must take my teeth out this time.

00:33:40.007 --> 00:33:41.297
The last time I lost.

00:33:41.317 --> 00:33:43.438
It's not an amusement park.

00:33:43.498 --> 00:33:45.078
Stop it, both of you.

00:33:45.138 --> 00:33:48.309
It's a real castle built by, um...

00:33:48.369 --> 00:33:56.892
A German in 1817 the past many years ago.

00:33:56.952 --> 00:34:03.645
It was built by King Ludwig II in 1869 but it wasn't finished when he died.

00:34:03.705 --> 00:34:05.186
I'm impressed Pete.

00:34:05.246 --> 00:34:09.147
I didn't know you liked history and European history.

00:34:09.207 --> 00:34:13.199
Deadleg taught me everything while I was waiting for you all to get ready.

00:34:13.259 --> 00:34:15.870
He then tested me to check I knew the dates.

00:34:15.930 --> 00:34:17.521
Typical schoolteacher.

00:34:17.582 --> 00:34:20.313
What a nice man he is.

00:34:20.373 --> 00:34:24.375
And his name is Deadleg, not Deadleg.

00:34:24.435 --> 00:34:27.677
Why hasn't he got a new wife or girlfriend?

00:34:27.697 --> 00:34:29.998
Oh, I'm free.

00:34:30.058 --> 00:34:32.581
Your mother lives in a fantasy world.

00:34:32.642 --> 00:34:37.277
No one with any intelligence, common sense, or glasses would want you.

00:34:37.337 --> 00:34:39.050
Not now, Pete.

00:34:39.110 --> 00:34:41.472
Park over there, under the trees.

00:34:41.532 --> 00:34:42.343
Okay.

00:34:42.403 --> 00:34:48.806
Okay.

00:34:48.866 --> 00:34:55.248
Come on, then.

00:34:55.308 --> 00:34:56.628
To the castle.

00:34:56.689 --> 00:34:58.620
It's Miles, Mum.

00:34:58.680 --> 00:35:02.282
It says on this notice that it's a 30 minute walk.

00:35:02.342 --> 00:35:03.873
Can't we go by taxi?

00:35:03.933 --> 00:35:04.524
Sure.

00:35:04.584 --> 00:35:06.214
The use of today.

00:35:06.274 --> 00:35:08.326
A bit of fresh air is good for you.

00:35:08.386 --> 00:35:10.748
I want to stay in the car with Boris.

00:35:10.808 --> 00:35:11.758
You all go.

00:35:11.818 --> 00:35:13.429
I can take Boris for a walk.

00:35:13.489 --> 00:35:14.050
No.

00:35:14.110 --> 00:35:15.640
You are right.

00:35:15.700 --> 00:35:17.202
You stay there.

00:35:17.262 --> 00:35:18.472
Come on, Mum.

00:35:18.533 --> 00:35:20.471
Pete.

00:35:20.532 --> 00:35:23.410
Come on out, little thing.

00:35:23.471 --> 00:35:27.221
You don't want to see a stupid castle, do you?

00:35:27.282 --> 00:35:29.582
No.

00:35:29.643 --> 00:35:32.804
Where's my mobile?

00:35:32.864 --> 00:35:38.546
Here it is.

00:35:38.606 --> 00:35:44.329
Mike, it's me.

00:35:44.389 --> 00:35:47.523
No, I'm at some boring castle.

00:35:47.583 --> 00:35:49.874
I wish I was with you.

00:35:49.934 --> 00:35:51.906
Course I love you.

00:35:51.926 --> 00:35:54.378
I'll see you tomorrow at school.

00:35:54.438 --> 00:35:57.469
We can get...

00:35:57.530 --> 00:36:02.981
Oh, at last the castle.

00:36:03.041 --> 00:36:05.601
Oh, what a long walk.

00:36:05.662 --> 00:36:06.982
All uphill.

00:36:07.042 --> 00:36:10.843
It's a lovely day and the air is so fresh.

00:36:10.903 --> 00:36:13.443
Germans are very strange people.

00:36:13.503 --> 00:36:15.224
What do you mean now?

00:36:15.284 --> 00:36:17.974
Well look, those two people there.

00:36:18.034 --> 00:36:21.237
There's no snow here, but they've got ski sticks.

00:36:21.298 --> 00:36:23.102
Lost your skis.

00:36:23.162 --> 00:36:24.892
So rude.

00:36:24.952 --> 00:36:26.844
But what's that point?

00:36:26.904 --> 00:36:28.506
They look so stupid.

00:36:28.566 --> 00:36:30.537
I think it's a new sport.

00:36:30.597 --> 00:36:32.698
Perhaps I can try it back home.

00:36:32.758 --> 00:36:37.279
If you try that in Stratford, I think you'll be arrested and put in a straight jacket.

00:36:37.339 --> 00:36:39.286
That's not a bad idea.

00:36:39.346 --> 00:36:40.627
Perhaps you should try it.

00:36:40.647 --> 00:36:42.287
Don't listen to him, Mum.

00:36:42.347 --> 00:36:44.238
It's a very healthy sport.

00:36:44.298 --> 00:36:45.948
It's very popular here.

00:36:46.008 --> 00:36:49.139
I think it's called Nordic Walking.

00:36:49.199 --> 00:36:50.509
Oh, no.

00:36:50.569 --> 00:36:51.990
There's a long queue.

00:36:52.050 --> 00:36:53.690
Blasted tourists.

00:36:53.750 --> 00:36:55.571
They're all bloody Japanese.

00:36:55.631 --> 00:36:57.131
There's hundreds of them.

00:36:57.191 --> 00:36:58.522
It's like London.

00:36:58.582 --> 00:37:02.093
They all look the same to me with their red caps and name tags.

00:37:02.153 --> 00:37:04.450
Come on, to the front.

00:37:04.510 --> 00:37:06.336
Excuse me.

00:37:06.396 --> 00:37:07.247
Thank you.

00:37:07.307 --> 00:37:09.428
Yeah, we just want to get through.

00:37:09.488 --> 00:37:10.478
Excuse me.

00:37:10.538 --> 00:37:11.348
I'm English.

00:37:11.408 --> 00:37:13.969
We're very important guests.

00:37:14.029 --> 00:37:17.140
And you are not important.

00:37:17.200 --> 00:37:18.581
Yes.

00:37:18.641 --> 00:37:19.091
Yes.

00:37:19.151 --> 00:37:21.002
Pollota, very good car.

00:37:21.062 --> 00:37:23.122
You'll make good TVs, too.

00:37:23.183 --> 00:37:24.783
Let us do, please.

00:37:24.843 --> 00:37:27.064
There we are, front of the queue.

00:37:27.124 --> 00:37:27.764
Come on.

00:37:27.824 --> 00:37:32.181
Guided pour in 10 minutes.

00:37:32.241 --> 00:37:37.930
You should be a little more understanding, Pete.

00:37:37.990 --> 00:37:40.722
Yes, and not so arrogant.

00:37:40.782 --> 00:37:41.904
Excuse me.

00:37:41.964 --> 00:37:44.096
You're not who built Castle?

00:37:44.156 --> 00:37:45.858
Oh, yes.

00:37:45.918 --> 00:37:49.180
Ludwig II in 1869.

00:37:49.240 --> 00:37:51.162
He died before it was finished.

00:37:51.223 --> 00:37:53.294
Oh, your expert on Castle.

00:37:53.354 --> 00:37:55.016
Ah, yes, a bit.

00:37:55.076 --> 00:37:56.668
I live in the castle.

00:37:56.728 --> 00:37:57.629
Pete.

00:37:57.689 --> 00:37:58.510
Don't.

00:37:58.570 --> 00:37:59.831
Just a bit of fun.

00:37:59.891 --> 00:38:01.642
You live in castle?

00:38:01.702 --> 00:38:03.382
Oh, wonderful.

00:38:03.442 --> 00:38:07.134
My wife wants to know if she can sit on throne for photo.

00:38:07.194 --> 00:38:08.955
Of course she can.

00:38:09.015 --> 00:38:10.666
Don't worry about the rope.

00:38:10.726 --> 00:38:12.546
Just jump over it.

00:38:12.607 --> 00:38:15.298
Hal'd nine, does his mister loved.

00:38:15.358 --> 00:38:16.908
Come on.

00:38:16.968 --> 00:38:20.610
Sometimes you are very nasty.

00:38:20.670 --> 00:38:22.921
The poor Japanese couple.

00:38:22.981 --> 00:38:24.572
What fun.

00:38:24.632 --> 00:38:27.354
Why did I marry you, Pete?

00:38:27.414 --> 00:38:30.447
Because you love me dear.

00:38:30.507 --> 00:38:32.628
I said because...

00:38:32.668 --> 00:38:37.601
Nancy heard you the first time.

00:38:37.662 --> 00:38:42.715
In and about Munich.

00:38:42.775 --> 00:38:45.146
Come on this way.

00:38:45.206 --> 00:38:47.338
Do you know where we are going?

00:38:47.398 --> 00:38:49.420
Munich is such a big city.

00:38:49.480 --> 00:38:51.401
Of course I do.

00:38:51.461 --> 00:38:52.742
I'm a man.

00:38:52.802 --> 00:38:54.263
We don't need perhaps.

00:38:54.323 --> 00:38:56.552
We just know where we are going.

00:38:56.612 --> 00:38:58.152
I want to go shopping.

