00:53:23.581 --> 00:53:25.631
So, I crossed over the street.

00:53:25.691 --> 00:53:30.053
As I got to the other side, she started screaming and waving her stick.

00:53:30.113 --> 00:53:32.074
I don't see what's so funny.

00:53:32.134 --> 00:53:36.616
I thought maybe she's escaped from the loony bin, or maybe drank too much snaps.

00:53:36.676 --> 00:53:41.431
In Germany it is normal to wait at the traffic lights until the light turns green.

00:53:41.491 --> 00:53:44.353
Yes, but there weren't any cars.

00:53:44.413 --> 00:53:46.654
That doesn't matter, it's the law.

00:53:46.714 --> 00:53:50.146
Typical Germans, what a stupid law.

00:53:50.206 --> 00:53:52.878
Oh look, rowing boats.

00:53:52.938 --> 00:53:54.810
I want to go on the lake.

00:53:54.870 --> 00:53:58.101
Come on everyone, we can eat afterwards.

00:53:58.162 --> 00:53:59.682
That's a good idea.

00:53:59.743 --> 00:54:00.733
Let's go.

00:54:00.793 --> 00:54:04.896
Alright, you two peed.

00:54:04.956 --> 00:54:06.599
Guten tak.

00:54:06.659 --> 00:54:12.375
The avant ein rowing ship for ein our bitter danker.

00:54:12.435 --> 00:54:15.337
Your German is so good, Josie.

00:54:15.397 --> 00:54:17.208
It's wonderful you're with us.

00:54:17.268 --> 00:54:19.480
I don't know what we would have done without you.

00:54:19.540 --> 00:54:20.972
Stayed in England.

00:54:21.032 --> 00:54:23.544
It's important to meet other people.

00:54:23.604 --> 00:54:25.495
Get to know how they lived at.

00:54:25.555 --> 00:54:26.666
I don't see why.

00:54:26.686 --> 00:54:30.859
There's no better holiday than a week or two in Blackpool.

00:54:30.919 --> 00:54:33.010
It has everything you need.

00:54:33.070 --> 00:54:34.260
Except Sun.

00:54:34.321 --> 00:54:36.602
The Sun comes out on Sundays.

00:54:36.662 --> 00:54:37.912
Not when we're there.

00:54:37.972 --> 00:54:40.233
And we're there every year.

00:54:40.273 --> 00:54:42.234
Oh, I like it.

00:54:42.294 --> 00:54:43.625
Here we are.

00:54:43.685 --> 00:54:45.286
I want to roll.

00:54:45.346 --> 00:54:46.706
I want to roll.

00:54:46.766 --> 00:54:48.097
You're so first, Mum.

00:54:48.157 --> 00:54:50.458
Don't rock the boat.

00:54:50.518 --> 00:54:54.219
This is fun when everyone just sits down.

00:54:54.239 --> 00:54:55.840
Boris, lie down.

00:54:55.900 --> 00:54:59.742
Could you tell your mum that if she wants to roll, she needs to turn around.

00:54:59.802 --> 00:55:01.643
I don't know what to mean.

00:55:01.703 --> 00:55:03.444
Oh, absolutely.

00:55:03.484 --> 00:55:05.355
We're going backwards.

00:55:05.415 --> 00:55:07.076
Be careful, Mum.

00:55:07.136 --> 00:55:08.607
Oh, oh.

00:55:08.667 --> 00:55:09.608
Careful.

00:55:09.628 --> 00:55:11.268
This is fun.

00:55:11.328 --> 00:55:13.450
Don't knock the boat, Josie.

00:55:13.470 --> 00:55:15.151
Give the oars to me.

00:55:15.211 --> 00:55:17.072
You have no idea.

00:55:17.132 --> 00:55:19.543
No, I want to row.

00:55:19.603 --> 00:55:20.274
I want them.

00:55:20.314 --> 00:55:22.405
You are a danger to civilisation.

00:55:22.465 --> 00:55:23.886
Stupid, the two of you.

00:55:23.946 --> 00:55:25.797
You're behaving just like children.

00:55:25.817 --> 00:55:26.877
I want them.

00:55:26.917 --> 00:55:28.100
Give them to me.

00:55:28.160 --> 00:55:29.552
I've had enough.

00:55:29.612 --> 00:55:33.254
Can we go back to the shore now?

00:55:33.314 --> 00:55:36.056
I don't believe it.

00:55:36.116 --> 00:55:37.636
What a holiday.

00:55:37.696 --> 00:55:39.237
Your mother started it.

00:55:39.297 --> 00:55:40.417
No, I did.

00:55:40.477 --> 00:55:41.447
Both of you.

00:55:41.508 --> 00:55:44.439
Now, let me get out of this boat.

00:55:44.499 --> 00:55:45.640
Be careful.

00:55:45.700 --> 00:55:46.670
Don't do that.

00:55:46.730 --> 00:55:47.920
No, the other way.

00:55:47.980 --> 00:55:49.671
Put one foot on the bank.

00:55:49.731 --> 00:55:50.712
No, don't grab.

00:55:50.772 --> 00:55:52.653
Throw the other way.

00:55:52.713 --> 00:55:53.663
Which way?

00:55:53.723 --> 00:55:54.994
I'm confused.

00:55:55.054 --> 00:55:57.335
Give them to me, you silly old bat.

00:55:57.355 --> 00:56:02.676
No.

00:56:02.736 --> 00:56:09.596
Oh, thank you, Boris!

00:56:09.656 --> 00:56:11.918
Somebody's here to save me!

00:56:11.978 --> 00:56:15.378
Oh, my leg!

00:56:15.438 --> 00:56:20.420
It hurts!

00:56:20.480 --> 00:56:23.812
Flying is better.

00:56:23.872 --> 00:56:26.622
Unbelievable.

00:56:26.682 --> 00:56:28.393
Unbelievable.

00:56:28.453 --> 00:56:30.183
All right, all right.

00:56:30.223 --> 00:56:31.344
What a family.

00:56:31.404 --> 00:56:32.564
Unbelievable.

00:56:32.624 --> 00:56:34.625
Can you stop saying unbelievable, dear?

00:56:34.685 --> 00:56:38.032
Well, it is rather unbelievable.

00:56:38.092 --> 00:56:39.360
I know.

00:56:39.420 --> 00:56:40.981
Your mother started it.

00:56:41.041 --> 00:56:42.052
No I didn't.

00:56:42.112 --> 00:56:43.584
How is the leg Nancy?

00:56:43.644 --> 00:56:44.456
Does it hurt?

00:56:44.516 --> 00:56:45.687
Yes it does.

00:56:45.747 --> 00:56:46.568
A lot.

00:56:46.628 --> 00:56:51.555
My friend Marcus at the Bingo Club lost his leg on a Tuesday.

00:56:51.615 --> 00:56:52.496
I'm sorry.

00:56:52.556 --> 00:56:54.088
My friend Marcus.

00:56:54.148 --> 00:56:57.029
I heard you the first time but why are you telling us?

00:56:57.089 --> 00:56:59.829
I just wanted to make Nancy feel better.

00:56:59.889 --> 00:57:05.983
You think telling a story about some old codger losing his leg on a Tuesday is going to make Nancy feel better?

00:57:06.043 --> 00:57:06.764
Yes.

00:57:06.824 --> 00:57:09.726
He found it again on Wednesday.

00:57:09.786 --> 00:57:12.547
Your English are so funny.

00:57:12.608 --> 00:57:15.872
Thank you, Mum, for trying to cheer me up.

00:57:15.932 --> 00:57:19.615
What's more worrying is how we are all going to get home tomorrow.

00:57:19.675 --> 00:57:24.478
There's not enough space in the car for four people, the luggage and Nancy's leg.

00:57:24.538 --> 00:57:25.518
I know.

00:57:25.578 --> 00:57:27.640
Nancy can stay with us a bit longer.

00:57:27.700 --> 00:57:29.370
That's a good idea, Heidi.

00:57:29.430 --> 00:57:37.275
I am very happy to have you in my house for a few days and then I can put you on a flight to London, maybe next week.

00:57:37.335 --> 00:57:39.208
But I couldn't.

00:57:39.268 --> 00:57:41.912
That's decided then.

00:57:41.972 --> 00:57:43.675
But no more discussion.

00:57:43.735 --> 00:57:44.897
That's organized then.

00:57:44.957 --> 00:57:45.398
Good.

00:57:45.458 --> 00:57:49.338
Come on Heidi, let's go and organize something to eat.

00:57:49.398 --> 00:57:53.086
I don't remember saying yes to dead leg to you.

00:57:53.147 --> 00:57:57.200
No, I didn't either, but he's very...

00:57:57.260 --> 00:57:57.970
German.

00:57:58.031 --> 00:58:01.994
He's very German, likes to organise everything and everyone.

00:58:02.054 --> 00:58:05.186
It's a good idea, Nancy, don't you think?

00:58:05.246 --> 00:58:10.300
Twelve hours in that car with your leg bandaged is not a good idea.

00:58:10.360 --> 00:58:14.693
And I'm sure the two of you can have a nice time together.

00:58:14.753 --> 00:58:18.475
I don't want to go home and I don't want to go in that car either.

00:58:18.535 --> 00:58:20.646
You can't stay here, Josie.

00:58:20.706 --> 00:58:25.089
Why don't Josie and I stay here in extra week with you, Nancy?

00:58:25.149 --> 00:58:25.489
Look.

00:58:25.549 --> 00:58:26.860
Awesome idea, Gran.

00:58:26.920 --> 00:58:27.240
But please.

00:58:27.260 --> 00:58:29.571
Then we can all fly back to England together.

00:58:29.631 --> 00:58:30.972
In an aeroplane?

00:58:31.032 --> 00:58:31.922
Yes, Gran.

00:58:31.942 --> 00:58:33.353
That's normally how you fly.

00:58:33.413 --> 00:58:36.045
I always wanted to go in a flying machine.

00:58:36.065 --> 00:58:36.995
Me, too.

00:58:37.055 --> 00:58:38.356
It's a great idea.

00:58:38.416 --> 00:58:38.716
But...

00:58:38.776 --> 00:58:39.847
Sunshine, she's ready.

00:58:39.887 --> 00:58:40.377
Come on.

00:58:40.437 --> 00:58:44.529
Can Josie and I stay here with Nancy for another week?

00:58:44.589 --> 00:58:46.210
Of course, a nice idea.

00:58:46.230 --> 00:58:47.370
Cool!

00:58:47.430 --> 00:58:50.160
Then we can fly back together.

00:58:50.220 --> 00:58:52.600
What about me?

00:58:52.660 --> 00:58:55.601
You told me you never wanted to fly.

00:58:55.661 --> 00:58:56.812
Remember?

00:58:56.872 --> 00:59:01.233
Yes, but your three ladies can fly back with one of those cheap airlines.

00:59:01.293 --> 00:59:02.383
It's not expensive.

00:59:02.443 --> 00:59:03.384
Wonderful.

00:59:03.444 --> 00:59:05.314
What a lovely idea.

00:59:05.374 --> 00:59:07.505
I don't know how to thank you.

00:59:07.565 --> 00:59:09.606
I'm sure you can think of something, Mum.

00:59:09.666 --> 00:59:11.706
What do you mean, Josephine?

00:59:11.766 --> 00:59:14.117
Nothing, Mum, nothing.

00:59:14.177 --> 00:59:17.268
Anyway, Pete, you need to pack the car.

00:59:17.328 --> 00:59:19.859
It's a long journey to the ferry port.

00:59:19.919 --> 00:59:21.298
But...

00:59:21.359 --> 00:59:23.120
Alright.

00:59:23.180 --> 00:59:24.772
I get the message.

00:59:24.832 --> 00:59:25.642
Right.

00:59:25.702 --> 00:59:26.603
Okay.

00:59:26.664 --> 00:59:29.677
I'm driving home on my own with Boris.

00:59:29.737 --> 00:59:31.039
Super.

00:59:31.099 --> 00:59:34.363
Terrific.

00:59:34.423 --> 00:59:43.756
Pete's trip home.

00:59:43.816 --> 00:59:51.955
Now, dear, are you sure you have everything?

00:59:52.015 --> 00:59:54.966
Yes, dear, I packed the car myself.

00:59:55.026 --> 00:59:56.537
That's what I mean.

00:59:56.557 --> 00:59:58.788
Do you want me to check it for you?

00:59:58.848 --> 01:00:00.539
I'm not totally useless.

01:00:00.599 --> 01:00:02.990
No, dear, of course you're not.

01:00:03.050 --> 01:00:10.354
Hope the three of, er, two of you have a nice journey, Dad.

01:00:10.414 --> 01:00:12.169
What?

01:00:12.229 --> 01:00:13.404
Three.

01:00:13.464 --> 01:00:15.376
What are you talking about, Josie?

01:00:15.436 --> 01:00:17.698
There's only me and Boris alone.

01:00:17.758 --> 01:00:19.600
Er, yes Dad, are you?

01:00:19.660 --> 01:00:20.570
Forgot.

01:00:20.630 --> 01:00:21.652
Forgot?

01:00:21.712 --> 01:00:23.163
What's our family?

01:00:23.224 --> 01:00:24.574
Alright.

01:00:24.634 --> 01:00:26.046
Goodbye.

01:00:26.107 --> 01:00:27.538
Have a nice week.

01:00:27.598 --> 01:00:29.760
Phone me if you have time.

01:00:29.820 --> 01:00:33.293
Bye!

01:00:33.353 --> 01:00:38.206
I hope he's alright by himself.

01:00:38.266 --> 01:00:41.076
He's happiest when he's with his car.

01:00:41.136 --> 01:00:44.988
Yes, but what were you talking about, Josie?

01:00:45.048 --> 01:00:46.008
Sorry, Mum.

01:00:46.068 --> 01:00:49.849
Something about the three of you having a nice journey?

01:00:49.909 --> 01:00:51.740
Er, nothing, Mum.

01:00:51.800 --> 01:00:53.820
You didn't, did you?

01:00:53.840 --> 01:00:55.740
I didn't, what?

01:00:55.801 --> 01:00:58.441
Where's that rat of yours?

01:00:58.501 --> 01:00:59.642
Oh, I'm not sure.

01:00:59.662 --> 01:01:01.702
I think he's in a box.

01:01:01.762 --> 01:01:04.810
And where's the box, Josephine?

01:01:04.870 --> 01:01:14.023
I think it, er, maybe, er, in Dad's car, er, maybe.

01:01:14.083 --> 01:01:18.986
Your father is going to get a very big shock when he gets home.

01:01:19.046 --> 01:01:22.748
I just hope that the customs in England don't stop him.

01:01:22.808 --> 01:01:28.311
If they do, then your father might be spending a long holiday in one of Her Majesty's prisons.

01:01:28.371 --> 01:01:30.152
I'm sure he'll be OK.

01:01:30.212 --> 01:01:31.763
I hope you're right, Josie.

01:01:31.823 --> 01:01:37.238
I hope you're right.

01:01:37.298 --> 01:01:41.982
Good morning, sir.

01:01:42.042 --> 01:01:43.833
Can I see your passport?

01:01:43.894 --> 01:01:45.224
Thank you, sir.

01:01:45.284 --> 01:01:47.646
And your dog's passport, please, sir?

01:01:47.706 --> 01:01:49.147
Oh, don't worry, officer.

01:01:49.207 --> 01:01:49.977
He's fine.

01:01:50.037 --> 01:01:52.409
He's not a terrorist.

01:01:52.429 --> 01:01:55.981
Your dog needs a passport, sir, to show he's been inoculated.

01:01:56.041 --> 01:01:57.572
He's fine.

01:01:57.612 --> 01:02:01.014
He hasn't been near any strange dogs in Germany.

01:02:01.074 --> 01:02:04.356
But there are one or two strange people there.

01:02:04.416 --> 01:02:05.447
I'm sorry, sir.

01:02:05.507 --> 01:02:06.407
It's the law.

01:02:06.467 --> 01:02:09.759
Your dog will have to be putting quarantine for six months.

01:02:09.819 --> 01:02:11.045
Six months?

01:02:11.106 --> 01:02:12.272
Oh, no.

01:02:12.332 --> 01:02:14.464
What's Nancy going to say when she gets home?

01:02:14.524 --> 01:02:15.586
She'll kill me.

01:02:15.646 --> 01:02:17.788
There must be something I can do.

01:02:17.848 --> 01:02:18.990
I'm sorry, sir.

01:02:19.050 --> 01:02:21.932
Can you bring your dog with me, sir?

01:02:21.993 --> 01:02:25.718
Problems with your breaks, sir?

01:02:25.778 --> 01:02:27.940
Er...

01:02:28.000 --> 01:02:28.650
I...

01:02:28.710 --> 01:02:29.191
Er...

